<Layout title="About Shahzad Akram" description="Meet Shahzad Akram: more than 15 years in SEO, franchise growth, website launches and e-commerce, combining strategic leadership with hands-on delivery.">
<article class="wrapper marketing">
<section class="hero">
<div class="hero-copy">
<p class="eyebrow">ABOUT SHAHZAD AKRAM</p>
<h1>SEO experience built through doing the work</h1>
<p>I’m Shahzad Akram, an SEO and digital growth specialist with more than 15 years’ experience across franchise businesses, lead generation and e-commerce.</p>
<p>I’ve built websites, grown businesses, investigated performance problems and led projects involving developers, agencies and international teams.</p>
<p>Today, my main focus is helping franchise and multi-location businesses connect search visibility with customer enquiries and sustainable website growth.</p>
<p class="actions"><a href="/contact/">Discuss working together</a> · <a href="/work/">Explore my work</a></p>
</div>
<img class="portrait" src="/shahzad-akram-portrait.png" alt="Shahzad Akram, SEO consultant" width="1122" height="1402" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
</section>
<section>
<h2>My current role</h2>
<p>I lead SEO and digital growth across World Options, Mail Boxes Etc. UK and PACK &amp; SEND UK, with responsibility for organic-search priorities and website performance across six websites.</p>
<p>The work spans national services, local franchise visibility and franchise recruitment. It includes approximately 191 physical store pages and 335 virtual service office pages, each contributing to a wider network.</p>
<p>My responsibilities bring together strategy and delivery: deciding what needs attention, coordinating improvements and reporting performance to senior stakeholders.</p>
<p>I work with marketing teams, franchisees, developers and external agencies to move those priorities forward.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>How I got here</h2>
<h3>Starting with websites and local enquiries</h3>
<p>My early experience involved managing websites and online lead generation for legal businesses.</p>
<p>That work introduced me to the relationship between search visibility and commercial enquiries. It also meant taking responsibility for the practical details: page content, website updates and helping people find the right service.</p>
<h3>Building a lead-generation business</h3>
<p>I later co-founded Sweetbox Media, where I built and ranked websites targeting competitive claims-related searches.</p>
<p>The business generated nearly £300,000 in turnover during its first two years. I personally handled SEO, websites, lead generation and commercial relationships alongside my business partner.</p>
<p>It gave me direct experience of building an audience and turning enquiries into a business, with responsibility for the outcome as well as the marketing activity.</p>
<h3>Developing broader digital experience</h3>
<p>My subsequent work included freelance SEO, website development, content and paid-search management.</p>
<p>These roles expanded the range of problems I worked on—from new websites needing a clear structure to established businesses needing better lead generation and measurement.</p>
<h3>Moving into franchise and multi-brand SEO</h3>
<p>I joined World Options as an SEO Specialist in January 2019 and moved into my current Head of SEO &amp; Digital Growth role in December 2020.</p>
<p>My responsibilities grew to include additional brands, franchise networks and international website projects.</p>
<p>That progression has shaped my specialism in businesses where search strategy needs to work across multiple websites, locations and stakeholders.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Experience beyond the audit</h2>
<p>I have led nine major website launches and migrations across the UK, US and Australia.</p>
<p>Those projects have involved platform selection, domain strategy, website architecture, hosting discussions, analytics and launch planning. I have worked across WordPress, Shopify, Squarespace and custom website environments.</p>
<p>My role often involves translating between different perspectives: what the business wants to achieve, what customers need and what the delivery team needs to implement.</p>
<p>That experience informs the advice I give. Recommendations need to account for the platform, people, budget and dependencies involved.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Building businesses of my own</h2>
<p>Alongside employed roles, I have developed and operated my own businesses.</p>
<p>One of those is Shilajit UK, which I launched in 2020 and built on Shopify. My responsibilities have included the website, SEO, content, advertising and international landing pages, alongside sourcing, inventory, customer service and fulfilment.</p>
<p>The business reached a peak month of £43,609.44 in revenue and 1,259 orders. These are total business sales figures, rather than revenue attributed solely to SEO.</p>
<p>Running a business adds useful perspective to consultancy. A website sits within a wider operation, and more traffic is only valuable when the customer journey and the business behind it can support that demand.</p>
<p><a href="/work/shilajit-uk/">Read the Shilajit UK case study</a></p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>What working with me looks like</h2>
<h3>Understand the objective first</h3>
<p>I start by establishing what you want to achieve and what is preventing progress.</p>
<p>That might be local customer acquisition, franchise recruitment, a technical issue or a planned website change. The objective shapes the work.</p>
<h3>Use the evidence available</h3>
<p>I review relevant search data, analytics, website behaviour and information from your team.</p>
<p>Where tracking is incomplete or the cause of a problem is uncertain, I make that clear and identify what would help resolve it.</p>
<h3>Set practical priorities</h3>
<p>I help distinguish urgent problems from useful improvements and longer-term opportunities.</p>
<p>The plan needs to reflect what your team can deliver, with clear responsibilities and dependencies.</p>
<h3>Stay involved in implementation</h3>
<p>Depending on the scope, I can make changes directly, prepare briefs or work with developers and agencies.</p>
<p>I review completed work and help resolve questions as they arise.</p>
<h3>Explain progress clearly</h3>
<p>I aim to make reporting useful to the people making decisions.</p>
<p>That means explaining what changed, what the evidence shows and what deserves attention next.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Where I can help</h2>
<h3>Franchise SEO</h3>
<p>Coordinate search strategy across national websites, local franchise pages and recruitment platforms.</p>
<p><a href="/franchise-seo/">Explore franchise SEO</a></p>
<h3>Local &amp; Multi-Location SEO</h3>
<p>Improve location pages, local business information and the route to the appropriate branch.</p>
<p><a href="/services/multi-location-seo/">Explore multi-location SEO</a></p>
<h3>Franchise Recruitment SEO</h3>
<p>Help prospective franchisees find and understand your opportunity through clearer content and website structure.</p>
<p><a href="/services/franchise-recruitment-seo/">Explore franchise recruitment SEO</a></p>
<h3>Technical SEO &amp; Website Migrations</h3>
<p>Investigate technical problems and bring SEO requirements into rebuilds, platform changes and launches.</p>
<p><a href="/services/technical-seo-migrations/">Explore technical SEO and migrations</a></p>
<h3>SEO Consultancy &amp; Leadership</h3>
<p>Get experienced support with priorities, strategy, delivery and performance reporting.</p>
<p><a href="/services/seo-consultancy/">Explore SEO consultancy</a></p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>What I write about</h2>
<p>I use this website to share practical work, case studies and lessons from building businesses.</p>
<p>Topics include technical SEO, analytics, franchise growth, website development and e-commerce. I’m interested in explaining how a problem was investigated and what the evidence showed, including where the first assumption turned out to be wrong.</p>
<p><a href="/blog/">Read the blog</a> · <a href="/seo/">Browse SEO guides</a></p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Let’s discuss your website</h2>
<p>If you need support with franchise SEO, a website project or a clearer plan for organic growth, tell me what you are working on.</p>
<p>I’ll reply personally so we can establish whether my experience fits what you need.</p>
<p><a href="/contact/">Discuss your project</a></p>
<p>Or email <a href="mailto:contact@shahzadakram.com">contact@shahzadakram.com</a>.</p>
